From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grant McNaught <1371263+gmcnaught@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 21:13:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 35/38] docs(render): fix stale bgplane comment describing the
 pre-fix single-plane design

Entities.cpp's comment above resident_static_before_animated() still
described the original (buggy) mechanism this branch's Tasks 1-5 just
fixed -- 'baked from EVERY layer's statics' and 'fire only once, on
whichever layer draws first' both describe the flattened-plane design
that caused bug #1, not the corrected base-layer-only design. Update it
to match reality.
---
 src/entities/Entities.cpp | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/entities/Entities.cpp b/src/entities/Entities.cpp
index 9b35002..7271588 100644
--- a/src/entities/Entities.cpp
+++ b/src/entities/Entities.cpp
@@ -1538,11 +1538,13 @@ void Entities::draw() {
       // through the gaps -- with zero cost, since this is just a call-order swap.
       //
       // [Phase 3b] resident_static_before_animated() flips this back for a renderer whose
-      // "static layer" is really a one-shot full-frame COPY of a plane baked from EVERY
-      // layer's statics (see MisterBlitterRenderer::resident_emit_static_layer): that COPY
-      // is latched to fire only once, on whichever layer draws first, so it MUST still run
-      // before any animated/entity draws this frame -- after would wipe out that layer's
-      // own just-drawn animated tiles.
+      // "static layer" is really a one-shot full-frame COPY of a plane baked from ONLY the
+      // map's BASE layer (map.get_min_layer(), latched as MisterBlitterRenderer's
+      // Impl::bg_base_layer -- see resident_begin_frame/resident_emit_static_layer): that
+      // COPY fires ONLY when this is the base layer, the one layer guaranteed to draw
+      // before anything else has drawn to the framebuffer this frame, so it MUST still run
+      // before that layer's own animated/entity draws. Every other layer always uses the
+      // per-bucket path below, unconditionally -- exactly as if BGPLANE were off.
       const bool _static_first = R.resident_static_before_animated(layer);
       if (_tilestatic && _static_first) {
         R.resident_emit_static_layer(layer);
